From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 05:23:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/apple-dart: describe the retained T8132 display DARTs
 per board

The DART driver leaves the two live internal display DARTs of the
MacBook Air (13-inch, M4) untouched until the guarded j713_dcp or
j713_display opt-in, and its DCP DART adoption reads the boot ADT, which
must name the J713 as its target.

The MacBook Pro (14-inch, M4) has the same two DARTs: its Apple device
tree (25G83 and 26B123 j604ap templates) gives dart-dcp at 0x30a340000
(SID 23) and dart-disp0 at 0x30a300000 (SID 0 scanout, SID 16 PIODMA),
interrupt 678 and the same VM base and size as the J713, and its root
target-type is "J604". Its DCP firmware is the same 26.6.2 image (UUID
81BAF476-679D-3CC0-8C6A-E6B6FA659D5E), which the ADT parser still
requires.

Move the machine test into a small board list and admit the J604 there
and in the ADT target-type check. The J713 behaviour is unchanged. On
the J604 these DARTs now take the same guarded path: without
CONFIG_APPLE_DART_J713_DCP the probe is refused, and without the
j713_dcp or j713_display parameter it returns -ENODEV, instead of
resetting a DART the firmware is using. No J604 device tree enables
these DARTs yet, so nothing probes them today.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart-dcp-format.h |  3 ++-
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c            | 21 +++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart-dcp-format.h b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart-dcp-format.h
index 5351da2a14..9ac3800379 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart-dcp-format.h
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart-dcp-format.h
@@ -110,7 +110,8 @@ static inline int dcp_adt_value(struct dcp_adt_tables *out, unsigned int kind,
 
 	if (kind == 1 && !strcmp(name, "target-type")) {
 		bit = 1;
-		if (length != 5 || memcmp(value, "J713", 5))
+		/* Boards with the retained T8132 internal display handoff. */
+		if (length != 5 || (memcmp(value, "J713", 5) && memcmp(value, "J604", 5)))
 			return -ENODEV;
 	} else if (kind == 3 && !strcmp(name, "compatible")) {
 		bit = 2;
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
index 9c020a623b..17619e172c 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -3912,6 +3912,23 @@ static void apple_dart_free_irq(struct apple_dart *dart)
 			apple_dart_display_irq_peers[i] = NULL;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Boards whose loader can hand over the running internal display: the DCP
+ * firmware DART (SID23) at 0x30a340000 and the scanout/PIODMA frontend DART
+ * (SID0/SID16) at 0x30a300000. The J604 Apple device tree describes the same
+ * two DARTs as the J713 (registers, interrupt, SIDs, VM ranges).
+ */
+static const char *const apple_dart_retained_display_boards[] = {
+	"apple,j713",
+	"apple,j604",
+	NULL
+};
+
+static bool apple_dart_retained_display_board(void)
+{
+	return of_machine_compatible_match(apple_dart_retained_display_boards);
+}
+
 static int apple_dart_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	int ret, sid;
@@ -3927,12 +3944,12 @@ static int apple_dart_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	bool j713_display, j713_radio;
 
 	/*
-	 * The J713 internal display DARTs are live: DCP firmware (SID23) and
+	 * The retained internal display DARTs are live: DCP firmware (SID23) and
 	 * the scanout/PIODMA frontend (SID0/SID16) keep using them. Leave both
 	 * untouched until userspace, with its watchdog armed, opts in.
 	 */
 	res = platform_get_resource(pdev, IORESOURCE_MEM, 0);
-	j713_display = res && !tunneled && of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j713") &&
+	j713_display = res && !tunneled && apple_dart_retained_display_board() &&
 		of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t8132-dart") &&
 		(res->start == 0x30a300000ULL || res->start == 0x30a340000ULL);
 	/* The J713 radio DART's fault interrupt is not described by its loader. */
